;
; steamclient.def -- the guest i386 export table for steamclient.dll.
;
; The same list, and the same ordinals, as ../steamclient64/steamclient64.def:
; Proton ships one lsteamclient.spec for both widths and the export NAMES are
; identical and undecorated in both of its built DLLs (measured with
; llvm-readobj on Proton-Power9's own i386-windows and x86_64-windows builds).
; It is a separate file only because a .def carries the module's own name on
; its LIBRARY line, and this one is steamclient.dll.
;
; Ordinals are copied from Proton's proton/lsteamclient.spec, which is
; itself the export layout the real Valve steamclient64.dll has (see that
; file's own header comment).  Only its "cdecl" entries are listed here.
; Its "stub" entries -- the overwhelming majority of the spec, covering
; interfaces and GameOverlayRenderer entry points this port does not
; implement -- are deliberately left OUT of this table, not exported as
; stubs: a probe for one of them should fail the way an absent export
; fails (GetProcAddress returns NULL, dlopen-style lazy binding never
; touches it), not the way a present-but-broken one fails.
;
; The spec's one remaining cdecl entry, steamclient_init_registry, is
; marked "-private" there.  Wine's own winebuild treats FLAG_PRIVATE
; exports as present in the binary but absent from the export table (see
; is_private handling in tools/winebuild/spec32.c); simply not listing it
; here has the same effect, so it is not in this table either.
;
; The four __wine_steamrpc_* entries are not in Proton's spec at all -- they
; are this port's own, driven by ppc64le/steamapi/check-steam-bridge.sh: the
; marshaller self-test, the synthetic-callback hook that lets the gate prove
; callback delivery with no Steam client, the DOS<->unix path probe, and the
; deliberate buffer overrun that proves the helper's red zone catches a
; too-small marshal descriptor instead of dying of it.  They
; are exported (rather than built into a separate test-only DLL) so that the
; gate exercises the same binary that ships, not a look-alike.  A game cannot
; reach any of them by accident: nothing in Steamworks has these names, and
; the two that talk to the helper do nothing until called.
;
; Copyright 2026 the ppc64le port authors
;
; This library is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it
; under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License as published by
; the Free Software Foundation; either version 2.1 of the License, or (at
; your option) any later version.
;
LIBRARY steamclient.dll
EXPORTS
Breakpad_SteamMiniDumpInit @1
Breakpad_SteamSetAppID @2
Breakpad_SteamSetSteamID @3
Breakpad_SteamWriteMiniDumpSetComment @4
Breakpad_SteamWriteMiniDumpUsingExceptionInfoWithBuildId @5
CreateInterface @6
Steam_BGetCallback @8
Steam_FreeLastCallback @15
Steam_GetAPICallResult @30
Steam_ReleaseThreadLocalMemory @35
Steam_IsKnownInterface
Steam_NotifyMissingInterface
__wine_steamrpc_selftest
__wine_steamrpc_inject
__wine_steamrpc_pathtest
__wine_steamrpc_overrun
